    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling output today, anchored by the elite speed-power combo of **Trea Turner** (75.08) and the aggressive outfield presence of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.50). **Trea Turner** remains our premier start against Alcantara, as his history of success against the right-hander combined with the leadoff slot provides the optimal environment for stolen base opportunities, our scarcest category. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** boasts a high score driven by favorable park dimensions and wind conditions; however, he bears a 43% rain risk, which makes him the most volatile asset in today's lineup. For reliable production, we are leaning heavily on **Kazuma Okamoto** (69.87) and **Kyle Schwarber** (69.22), both of whom benefit from significant platoon advantages and superior order positioning to maximize run production.\n\nTactically, we have favored **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) and **Christian Yelich** (62.60) over potential bench options, as their respective matchups against Ritchie and Williams offer the best path to efficiency despite modest SP_xERA figures. The most difficult decision this morning involved **Lars Nootbaar**, who barely missed the cut with a 50.08 score. While **Lars Nootbaar** offers a solid xwOBA and benefit from outward wind, he was ultimately benched because the projected efficiency of **Carson Benge**\u2014despite a platoon disadvantage\u2014remains higher due to his leadoff role and park factors. While **Junior Caminero** (55.21) remains in the UTIL slot to provide power, his score is suppressed by the difficult matchup against Ohtani; he remains on a short leash should the early innings suggest he is overmatched. We are also monitoring **Dillon Dingler** (46.60), as his start is contingent on his ability to mitigate the platoon penalty against Lambert.",
